{"html":"<p>Desktop Rust forgives mistakes; firmware does not. This project builds a real\nsensor node: reads temperature and humidity over I2C, buffers when the network is\ndown, publishes over MQTT, sleeps at 20 µA, and updates itself over the air.</p>\n<p><strong>What it is:</strong> an <code>embassy</code> firmware for an ESP32-C3 or STM32 board, plus a small\nRust gateway that receives the readings and writes them to Postgres.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-you-learn\">What you learn</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Skill</th>\n<th>Where it comes from</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>no_std</code> discipline</td>\n<td>no allocator, fixed buffers, <code>defmt</code> logging</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Async on bare metal</td>\n<td><code>embassy-executor</code>, timers, interrupts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Power budgets</td>\n<td>deep sleep, wake sources, measuring µA</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Offline resilience</td>\n<td>ring buffer in flash, at-least-once publish</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>OTA safely</td>\n<td>A/B partitions, signature check, rollback</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"milestones\">Milestones</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Ship</th>\n<th>Done when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Blink</td>\n<td>the LED blinks without a HAL panic</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Read the sensor</td>\n<td><code>defmt::info!</code> prints real temperature</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Publish</td>\n<td>the gateway logs an MQTT message</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Sleep</td>\n<td>average draw under 100 µA</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Buffer</td>\n<td>10 minutes offline, nothing lost</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Update</td>\n<td>new firmware over the air, old one kept for rollback</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"crates\">Crates</h2>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"toml\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"toml\" data-