></figure>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Gotcha:</strong> <code>I2c::new_blocking</code> in an async task blocks the executor for the\nduration of the transfer (~1 ms at 100 kHz). Use <code>I2c::new</code> with DMA and\n<code>.await</code> the transfer, or accept the stall — but know which you chose.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"sleeping-is-the-whole-product\">Sleeping is the whole product</h2>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">use</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> embassy_stm32</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">low_power</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">StopMode</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">;</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"> </span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// between readings, go to STOP2: ~1.1 µA on an STM32L4, RTC keeps running</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">StopMode</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\">enter</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">()</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">.await</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">;</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>State</th>\n<th>Current</th>\n<th>Battery (2000 mAh)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>awake, radio on</td>\n<td>80 mA</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>awake, sensor only</td>\n<td>4 mA</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>stop mode</td>\n<td>1.1 µA</td>\n<td>~2 years</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>60 s wake + 2 s radio</td>\n<td>~120 µA avg</td>\n<td>~1.9 years</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Measure it. A $10 USB power meter in line with the board turns \"should be low\npower\" into a number you can defend.</p>\n<h2 id=\"buffering-when-the-network-is-gone\">Buffering when the network is gone</h2>\n<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=\"\"><pre tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\"><code data-language=\"rust\" data-theme=\"github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"display: grid;\"><span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">use</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> heapless</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">{</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Deque</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Vec</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">};</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"> </span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">#[derive(serde</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Serialize</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">)]</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">struct</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> Reading</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> { t</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> i16</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, rh</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> u16</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, ts</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> u32</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> }   </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// fixed point, no floats on the wire</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"> </span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#768390\">// 128 readings * 8 bytes = 1 KB of RAM — survive a 2-hour outage</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">static</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> mut</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> RING</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> Deque</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Reading</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, 128> </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> Deque</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\">new</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">();</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>Flush the ring on reconnect, oldest first. Each reading carries a sequence number\nso the gateway can drop duplicates — the same idempotency rule as module 04.04,\none layer down.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ota-without-bricking-the-device\">OTA without bricking the device</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Two flash slots: <code>slot_a</code> (running) and <code>slot_b</code>.</li>\n<li>Download into the inactive slot, verifying a signature per chunk.</li>\n<li>Write a boot flag <strong>only after</strong> the whole image verifies.</li>\n<li>Boot the new slot with a \"trial\" counter; if it does not check in within 5\nminutes, the bootloader reverts.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Never overwrite the running image. Never flip the boot flag before verification.</p>\n<h2 id=\"stretch-goals\">Stretch goals</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>defmt</code> over RTT replaced by a binary log to flash.</li>\n<li>Sensor calibration coefficients stored in a config partition.</li>\n<li>A second core (ESP32) handling the radio while the first sleeps.</li>\n<li>A gateway dashboard showing battery voltage and last-seen.</li>\n<li>Run the same logic under <code>qemu-system-arm</code> in CI so firmware gets tests.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"demo-checklist\">Demo checklist</h2>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled> measured average current, with the meter visible in the video</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled> 10 minutes of readings buffered through an unplugged gateway</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled> an OTA update and a deliberate rollback</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled> <code>cargo build --release</code> binary under 128 KB</li>\n</ul>"}